@node Low Module
@chapter Low Module

The protocols in the low module provide the basic ``storage'' aspect of
a package system without additional logic or consideration of the
package system consistency rules:

@itemize

@item
Predicates for symbol and package objects and construction of symbol and
package objects

@item
Accessors for ``slots'' of symbols and packages

@item
Registration of package objects in the environment and retrieval of
package objects from the environment

@end itemize

The functions in this module accept only strings where names are
required and only symbol objects and package objects (not designators)
where symbols and packages are required.

@menu
* Low Symbol Functions::
* Low Package Functions::
* Low Package-symbol Relation Functions::
* Low Environment Functions::
@end menu

@node Low Symbol Functions
@section Low Symbol Functions

;;;; TODO: Old This file contains definitions of generic functions that are
;;;; called by various parts of Parcl.  Client code must supply a
;;;; method on each one of these functions, specialized to the
;;;; paticular client object it uses.

@defgena{symbolp,@lowpackage{}} client object

Return true if @var{object} is a symbol object @emph{in the package
system specified by @var{client}}.

The default method returns false for all objects so that clients can
simply define a method that is specialized to the respective client
class and the associated symbol class and returns true.
@end deffn

@defgena{symbol-name,@lowpackage{}} client symbol

Return the string that is the name of @var{symbol} @emph{in the package
system specified by @var{client}}.
@end deffn

@defgena{symbol-package,@lowpackage{}} client symbol

Return the package object that is the home package of @var{symbol} or
@code{nil} if @var{symbol} is uninterned @emph{in the package system
specified by @var{client}}.
@end deffn

@defgena{(setf symbol-package),@lowpackage{}} new-value client symbol

Set the home package of @var{symbol} to @var{new-value} @emph{in the
package system specified by @var{client}} and return @var{new-value}.

@var{new-value} is either @code{nil} or a package object.
@end deffn

@defgena{make-symbol,@lowpackage{}} client name package

Create and return a symbol object with name @var{name} and home package
@var{package} @emph{in the package system specified by @var{client}}.

@var{name} is a string and @var{package} is either @code{nil} or a
package object.  If @var{package} is @code{nil}, an uninterned symbol is
created and returned.
@end deffn

