@defgena{name,@lowpackage{}} client package

Return a string that is the name of the package object @var{package}
@emph{in the package system specified by @var{client}}.

This function can be used to implement and customize the standard
function @speclink{f,package-name}.
@end deffn

@defgena{(setf name),@lowpackage{}} new-value client package

Set the name of the package object @var{package} to the string
@var{new-value} @emph{in the package system specified by @var{client}}.

In accordance with the role of the low module, this function does not
check whether @var{new-name} is the name or the nickname of an existing
package nor does it register @var{package} in the environment under the
provided name.

